    "source": [
-    "As before, we can also estimate 2 metric that quantify FOD anisotropy:\n",
-    "- The anisotropy index (AI) following *(Jespersen et al. 2007)*, ranging from 1 for completely anistropic, to zero being isotropic.\n",
-    "- The norm of the laplacian of the spherical harmonics of the FOD, explored in e.g. *(Descoteaux et al. 2006)*, which is zero for isotropic FODs and increasingly positive for more anistropic FODs.\n",
-    "\n",
-    "It is relevant that AI is dependent on the value of the spherical mean of the FOD, but the Laplacian-norm is not."
+    "Now that the fractions are fitted and there are 3, we can also visualize them as an RGB image. Notice that the WM/GM/CSF areas are reasonably nicely segmented by the estimation itself."
    ]
